The grader fails when evaluating solutions used to create test kits. Root cause: `ReadLineAsync()` blocks indefinitely on prompts without trailing newlines (e.g., `Console.Write("Enter input: ")`), while the test kit generator captures all output including partial lines.

## Changes

### ExecutableManager.cs
Replaced line-based reading with time-based flushing:

```csharp
// Before: blocks on prompts without newlines
while ((line = await reader.ReadLineAsync()) != null)
{
    buffer.AppendLine(line);
}

// After: flushes partial output every 100ms
while (true)
{
    var readTask = reader.ReadAsync(charBuffer, 0, charBuffer.Length);
    var delayTask = lineBuffer.Length > 0 ? Task.Delay(100) : Task.Delay(Timeout.Infinite);
    var completed = await Task.WhenAny(readTask, delayTask);

    if (completed == readTask)
    {
        int charsRead = await readTask;
        if (charsRead == 0) break;
        // Process and flush on newline or after 100ms timeout
    }
}
```

**Flush triggers**:
- Newline character (preserves existing behavior)
- 100ms timeout (captures prompts)
- Stream end (captures remaining content)

### Impact
- Prompts without newlines now captured within 100ms
- Existing normalization already handles whitespace/case/BOM requirements
- No breaking changes to test suite format or comparison logic

